v 3
d riskscan: k-anonymity re-identification scan
d
d riskscan measures how exposed a de-identified dataset still is.
d It groups records by every combination of the quasi-identifiers
d you name, computes the cell size k for each record, and reports
d distinct cells, unique records (k=1), records below a threshold
d (default k<5), and a cell-size distribution. Options add an
d l-diversity check on a sensitive variable, a flag variable for
d at-risk records, and a listing of the smallest cells. Returned
d scalars let a do-file gate a data release programmatically.
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or newer. No other dependencies; the
d command reads only the data in memory and makes no network
d requests.
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260706
d
